00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:50.410
Chapter 20 Blade

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:00.010
1864 (Genji I)
June 5th, Early Morning

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:09.980
Yes, yes. Who is it?

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:11.360
It's terribly early.

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:23.120
Is it you, Master?

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:25.450
Where have you been?

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:27.290
There is something I
would like to report...

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:42.680
I'm so terribly sorry to disturb
you at such an early hour.

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:53.830
Well, well, this is quite
the elaborate joke.

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:54.810
A kimono...

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:58.700
I came to get one.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:02.790
The one set out all
prettily in the storefront.

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:05.580
I'm so sorry, I'm so sorry!

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:08.950
Washed all clean by the rain...

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:14.160
there's no soil on my body anymore,

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:18.010
but this alone just won't come out, so...

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:20.580
May I ask you to please leave?

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:23.250
This performance is in poor taste,
particularly so early in the day.

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:25.220
We find it difficult to
understand your actions.

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:30.450
In addition, I do not even know
why we might merit such a prank,

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:32.000
so if you will excuse me...

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:34.650
Mister Masuya...

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:37.110
How is your right arm doing?

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:42.500
You needn't worry. There was
nothing deadly on that blade.

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:44.370
And you can rest easy.

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:47.530
I need you to fess up to
all manner of things.

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:50.540
But for a while...

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:54.500
you'll have to suffer dull pain
like your wound being gouged

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:58.460
and have these purple blotches
on your skin. That's all.

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:00.080
Why...

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:01.950
Why are you alive?

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:05.040
With that many people,
they could not have possibly failed!

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:06.540
You cannot possibly...

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:08.470
be alive? No, of course not.

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:11.140
Who the hell...?

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:18.760
We are the Shinsengumi!

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:22.650
Thrift shop owner Kiemon Masuya,
also known as Shuntaro Furutaka!

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:26.780
You are plainly guilty of harboring
outlaws who would defy the Shogunate!

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:31.040
We will hear what you have
to say back at Headquarters.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:32.790
Come with us quietly.

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:39.250
You may cut down any who resist.

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:43.000
Do not allow a single soul to
escape from these premises!

00:05:01.450 --> 00:05:03.690
Master Okita...

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:12.080
Uh, um, Master Okita?

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:13.410
What is it?

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:18.060
Well, I just thought it was
unusual for you not to storm in

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:19.790
at a time like this.

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:25.420
I want to allow them to do as
they please, at least for today.

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:30.660
Masuya! No, Furutaka! Where is he?!

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:32.790
He should be around here somewhere!

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:34.510
Search every nook and cranny!

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:45.950
It was fortunate that the
Master was not here.

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:48.200
Right now, we must not waste any time in...

00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:08.110
The way she died...

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:12.750
was brutal.

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:14.750
Made sport of by those bastards,

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:17.320
she was covered with cuts
and bruises all over her body.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:21.050
You're in the way!

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:27.110
In the pouring rain...

00:06:29.540 --> 00:06:33.410
she'd been dumped like
she was less than trash.

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:37.370
With one eye put out,
her face was cruelly swollen...

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:39.770
Damn it!

00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:53.390
Her left arm was torn and the
broken bone was sticking out.

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:55.410
My fingers! My fingers!

00:06:55.410 --> 00:06:57.310
<i>At this rate...</i>

00:06:57.790 --> 00:06:59.000
<i>I'll be killed!</i>

00:06:59.000 --> 00:06:59.520
Hold it!

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:06.650
So, you'd rather get caught
than be killed... Is that it?

00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:11.290
I... only followed orders
from my superiors...

00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:14.370
and took care of a spy.

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:17.040
It's no different than what you do...

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:23.450
Not yet...

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:26.440
You're not nearly there yet...

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:29.840
What are you...?

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:32.180
For you to be begging for your life...

00:07:34.750 --> 00:07:36.390
you've still got a long way to go!

00:07:50.450 --> 00:07:51.710
<i>My sister...</i>

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:57.620
<i>never begged for her life,
to the very end, did she?</i>

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:07.130
Help...

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:11.910
Have you been told to kill me?

00:08:11.910 --> 00:08:13.790
No, right?

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:21.620
<i>My sister never begged for her life,
to the very end, did she?</i>

00:08:21.620 --> 00:08:25.950
<i>She just accepted all the
suffering and the humiliation,</i>

00:08:25.950 --> 00:08:29.450
<i>and passed on, proud of her fate as a spy.</i>

00:08:29.450 --> 00:08:32.510
<i>Proud enough for both of us...</i>

00:08:35.290 --> 00:08:39.370
I'm not really supposed to kill you, but...

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:40.490
Please...

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:49.500
I can't be a spy anymore!

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:03.000
Before dawn?!

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:04.080
Yeah.

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:08.190
The First and Sixth Units
went in with Soji in the lead.

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:13.780
<i>Susumu...</i>

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:17.240
<i>Don't tell me you...</i>

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:19.320
Susumu!

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:22.660
Where is he?

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:23.830
Susumu!

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:26.160
Quit yelling your head off
in a place like this.

00:09:26.950 --> 00:09:28.280
Susumu!

00:09:32.540 --> 00:09:34.570
It's all taken care of already.

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:38.110
Did you...?

00:09:40.540 --> 00:09:41.360
What?

00:09:45.370 --> 00:09:46.300
Did you...

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:49.370
do it after all...?

00:09:49.370 --> 00:09:50.520
You know...

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:53.690
Did you kill him?

00:09:54.620 --> 00:09:55.770
I couldn't...

00:09:56.910 --> 00:10:01.000
I couldn't hold back, so...

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:03.180
I sprained my fingers.

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:08.540
He probably won't be waking up for a while.

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:13.840
I actually came here meaning
to kill him, but...

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:17.340
Looks like I've come up short,
even at the very end...

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:18.590
But...

00:10:19.580 --> 00:10:24.160
But, even though I don't know if
that was for the better or not...

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:26.100
Still...

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:28.290
It makes me real happy!

00:10:28.290 --> 00:10:33.910
You didn't kill anyone,
so it makes me happy...

00:10:33.910 --> 00:10:34.960
And I'm sure, Ayu as well.

00:10:36.750 --> 00:10:38.000
Is that right?

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:40.940
Yeah!

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:45.910
Well, then, you go on back without me.

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:48.700
Or rather, don't come out here in
your night wear. It's embarrassing!

00:10:48.700 --> 00:10:50.080
Shut up!

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:52.750
I was in a hurry, so it's
not like I could help it!

00:10:57.710 --> 00:10:59.410
I see...

00:10:59.410 --> 00:11:02.050
So, we did not find him, after all.

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:06.950
There was a basement.
There may be other hidden rooms.

00:11:06.950 --> 00:11:10.910
We questioned all the ronin closely,
but there was no one suspicious...

00:11:10.910 --> 00:11:13.440
Please search the surrounding areas.

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:17.650
And send a message to
the Commander immediately,

00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:20.830
telling him Toshimaro Yoshida
has slipped through our fingers.

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:25.390
Suzu?

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:47.700
But man, we really just keep
running into each other, don't we?

00:11:47.700 --> 00:11:51.370
Like that time in Hyogo,
and that time in Shimabara.

00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:56.190
I'd always figured I'd see you again
around Shimabara or something.

00:11:56.190 --> 00:12:00.320
So, where did you want me to follow you to?

00:12:00.750 --> 00:12:04.300
Don't tell me it's this
abandoned house or something.

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:09.370
If you're bringing me out
to a place like this...

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:13.920
it means you want to talk
to me about something, right?

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:16.160
This is perfect.

00:12:16.160 --> 00:12:18.960
There's actually something
I want to ask you, too.

00:12:19.660 --> 00:12:21.040
<i>Don't talk!</i>

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:25.750
You know when your master
came to get you in Shimabara,

00:12:25.750 --> 00:12:28.170
was that actually...?

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:37.610
Tell me... Suzu...

00:12:40.330 --> 00:12:41.860
Suzu?

00:12:45.790 --> 00:12:47.490
What're you doing?

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:53.040
I'm asking you, what the
hell are you doing?!

00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:04.000
Come on, hurry it up!

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:05.870
What happened to Yoshida?

00:13:05.870 --> 00:13:08.390
It seems he slipped through our fingers.

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:10.590
I heard Mr. Hijikata's interrogating

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:20.610
Shinsengumi

00:13:10.590 --> 00:13:13.830
Masuya in the storehouse right now.

00:13:13.830 --> 00:13:16.910
Well, if it's the Demon Vice
Commander interrogating him...

00:13:16.910 --> 00:13:18.910
Pardon me for interrupting.

00:13:18.910 --> 00:13:20.610
Huh? What's up?

00:13:20.790 --> 00:13:22.410
Tetsu...

00:13:22.410 --> 00:13:24.280
Have you seen Tetsunosuke around?

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:27.580
Come to think of it, I haven't
seen him since this morning.

00:13:27.580 --> 00:13:32.160
Yes, he's neglecting even his page duties.
Where could he have gone?

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:37.330
Oh, that reminds me, he was seen
wandering around Masuya in night wear.

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:39.290
I heard it from some
guys in the Sixth Unit.

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:44.580
Oh-ho! Did he want to see the
Shinsengumi's big catch that badly?

00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:47.880
Aw, he didn't need to worry,
he'd eventually get the chance to...

00:13:48.080 --> 00:13:49.500
Hey!

00:13:50.790 --> 00:13:52.080
What's with him?

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:53.390
Who knows?

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:11.020
Put that thing away...

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:17.200
Come on, it's dangerous.

00:14:17.200 --> 00:14:19.180
Put your sword away.

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:22.590
I don't understand what you're doing.

00:14:46.070 --> 00:14:46.650
Suzu!

00:15:18.040 --> 00:15:19.870
Please wait...

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:20.810
Master...

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:33.200
Master... Yoshida...

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:36.730
So, you have some life left in you.

00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:41.890
Kiemon Masuya.

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:46.540
Real name: Masayasu Shuntaro Furutaka.

00:16:46.540 --> 00:16:50.080
On the face, you played the
good man running a thrift shop,

00:16:50.080 --> 00:16:54.160
but behind the scenes, you were a loyalist,

00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:58.330
who conspired with people from Choshu
and the West to harbor outlaw ronin.

00:16:58.330 --> 00:17:00.910
You probably thought you'd
disguised yourself well,

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:02.780
but you weren't thorough enough.

00:17:02.780 --> 00:17:05.410
We found weapons and
munitions in the basement,

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:10.120
and most helpfully, Aizu lanterns and a
compact signed by loyalist exclusionists.

00:17:12.250 --> 00:17:13.710
Let's hear it.

00:17:14.940 --> 00:17:18.430
This so-called scenario that
Master Yoshida wrote up.

00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:28.250
Oh, that reminds me.

00:17:28.250 --> 00:17:31.520
That pretty <i>kunoichi</i> you
guys were so nice to.

00:17:31.520 --> 00:17:36.570
It was almost surprising how stupid
you were about disposing of her.

00:17:37.250 --> 00:17:42.160
To think you'd ruin the delicate
balance you'd set up yourselves.

00:17:44.450 --> 00:17:47.830
Let me guess. Some idiot decided
not to look to the Master for guidance

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:50.250
and ended up letting things take a
turn for the absolute worst, right?

00:18:00.700 --> 00:18:03.720
Ah, no, that's not it.

00:18:07.200 --> 00:18:09.690
I know for certain now.

00:18:10.870 --> 00:18:13.700
Why the ronin weren't told to run,

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:17.740
in spite of there being a spy
acting as a watchdog...

00:18:18.040 --> 00:18:24.080
Why Yoshida alone had quietly disappeared
from Masuya without even telling you...

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:28.580
Eh, Furutaka?

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:30.500
Before the festival...
Before the festival...

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:32.200
even if you're an expendable pawn,

00:18:32.200 --> 00:18:34.060
if you burn brightly, maybe...

00:18:34.060 --> 00:18:38.300
maybe it'll make the
Master's sake taste a bit better.

00:18:38.660 --> 00:18:41.080
I...

00:18:41.080 --> 00:18:44.500
I did it for the Master...

00:20:29.370 --> 00:20:30.940
Master...

00:20:42.330 --> 00:20:43.800
Fire!

00:20:44.500 --> 00:20:47.160
Damn! Why's a rundown house on fire?!

00:20:47.160 --> 00:20:49.830
Someone, go call the fire brigade!

00:21:13.700 --> 00:21:16.750
Please, let me be wrong!

00:21:17.870 --> 00:21:20.700
This is bad! The fire's spreading fast!

00:21:20.700 --> 00:21:22.660
What the heck is going on?

00:21:22.660 --> 00:21:25.080
Water! Over here! This way!

00:21:25.080 --> 00:21:27.510
Isn't there someone inside?!

00:21:27.510 --> 00:21:28.970
Tetsu!

00:21:29.410 --> 00:21:31.040
What's the matter?

00:21:31.040 --> 00:21:33.330
Inside! There might be...

00:21:33.330 --> 00:21:36.080
My younger brother may be in there!

00:21:36.080 --> 00:21:37.410
What?!

00:21:37.410 --> 00:21:38.310
Hold it!

00:21:38.580 --> 00:21:39.830
It's no use!

00:21:39.830 --> 00:21:41.200
You won't make it in time now!

00:21:41.200 --> 00:21:42.580
Let go!

00:21:42.580 --> 00:21:44.190
Please let me go...

00:21:45.160 --> 00:21:48.290
Tetsu!

00:22:02.620 --> 00:22:06.910
<i>Maiku o nigirishime
hitto pareedo no onpareedo</i>

00:22:06.910 --> 00:22:10.470
<i>Hey, Jimmy, kibun wa doudai?</i>

00:22:10.470 --> 00:22:14.790
<i>Suteeji orireba sasuga no jentoruman</i>

00:22:14.790 --> 00:22:18.480
<i>Hey, Jimmy, kokoro mo kandai!</i>

00:22:18.480 --> 00:22:22.440
<i>Jimichi ga yue ni seikatsu sae mo jimi ni</i>

00:22:22.440 --> 00:22:26.290
<i>Kotsu-kotsu tsumiagemashou</i>

00:22:26.290 --> 00:22:30.290
<i>Jimichi ni yume ga kanaimasu you ni</i>

00:22:30.290 --> 00:22:34.040
<i>Kyou mo, Jimmy, ikimashou</i>

00:22:36.080 --> 00:22:39.660
<i>You got to fight for your money!
How you feeling, Jimmy?</i>

00:22:39.660 --> 00:22:43.630
<i>You got to fight for your dream,
it's all too much</i>

00:22:43.630 --> 00:22:47.500
<i>You got to fight for your money!
How you feeling, Jimmy?</i>

00:22:47.500 --> 00:22:51.640
<i>You got to fight for your dream,
it's all too much</i>

00:23:07.280 --> 00:23:11.120
<i>You got to fight for your money!
How you feeling, Jimmy?</i>

00:23:11.120 --> 00:23:15.080
<i>You got to fight for your dream,
it's all too much</i>

00:23:15.080 --> 00:23:19.000
<i>You got to fight for your money!
How you feeling, Jimmy?</i>

00:23:19.000 --> 00:23:23.330
<i>You got to fight for your dream,
it's all too much</i>

00:23:24.710 --> 00:23:27.920
Next Peacemaker Kurogane

00:23:25.410 --> 00:23:29.330
<i>Tetsu, things have really come
to a head while you were gone.</i>

00:23:29.330 --> 00:23:32.830
<i>Everyone at Headquarters is out
for blood, getting ready for the raid.</i>

00:23:32.830 --> 00:23:37.690
<i>Next time, Peacemaker Kurogane,
Chapter 21: "Battle Array."</i>

00:23:36.810 --> 00:23:39.690
